======================================================================================================================
FOOTING: canonical   a_0 = 9.360e-11 m/s^2
======================================================================================================================
  g_int/a_0: 5th 0.0249, median 0.1251, 95th 0.5606
  SATURATED prediction B: median 1.314, 5-95% 1.017-1.685
  ISOLATED prediction nu(g_int): median 3.356, 5-95% 1.897-6.848
  observed alpha_vir: median 5.852, 5-95% 1.549-43.168

  [SELF-GRAVITATING SUBSAMPLE]  M > 1e4 Msun and Sigma > 30 Msun/pc^2: N = 1327
     median alpha_vir = 3.729
     SATURATED law requires 1.170;  ISOLATED MOND requires 2.269;  Newton requires 1.000
     (the absolute value is NOT the verdict: alpha_vir carries the whole X_CO scale, d log alpha_vir/d log X_CO = -1.000)

  [SHAPE TEST 1] d log alpha_vir / d log g_int over 1.84 dex of internal acceleration, N = 1327
     measured -0.418 +- 0.034
     SATURATED law and Newton both predict 0.000 (no dependence on the cloud's own field)
     ISOLATED MOND predicts -0.500 in the deep limit

     MONTE CARLO CONTROL (bug pattern 5).  Build synthetic clouds that obey each hypothesis
     EXACTLY, then add the real measurement errors and re-measure the same slope.
       newton     truth -> estimator returns slope -0.400 +- 0.016
       saturated  truth -> estimator returns slope -0.427 +- 0.017
       isolated   truth -> estimator returns slope -0.623 +- 0.014
       DATA                                        -0.418 +- 0.034
     separation between the two MOND branches after the induced correlation: 0.197 in slope
  [PASS] the Monte Carlo separates SATURATED from ISOLATED MOND by more than the data's error bar, so shape test 1 is identified rather than degenerate  [CAN FAIL]   (branch separation 0.197 vs 3 sigma_data = 0.101)
     -> data are 0.5 sigma from Newton, 0.2 sigma from the SATURATION law, 5.7 sigma from ISOLATED MOND

  [SHAPE TEST 2] the Galactocentric lever.  B depends on R_gal ALONE, so at fixed surface
     density and fixed heliocentric distance (hence fixed physical resolution) alpha_vir must
     track B(R_gal).  Matched cells in (log Sigma, log D) remove both confounds.
     34 matched cells; inverse-variance combined slope of log alpha_vir on log B:
       -2.734 +- 0.099    [SATURATION law: +1.000;  Newton: 0.000]
       -> 37.8 sigma from the law, 27.6 sigma from Newton
       !! BOTH hypotheses are excluded at > 5 sigma.  A slope of -2.734 is outside
          anything either theory can produce, so this estimator is measuring a SYSTEMATIC,
          not physics.  Shape test 2 is UNIDENTIFIED and is not reported as a verdict.
     UNMATCHED (careless) version for contrast: +0.171 +- 0.103 -- the difference from
     the matched value is the size of the resolution/selection confound, not physics.
     DIAGNOSIS -- which factor of alpha_vir = 5 sigma_V^2/(pi G Sigma R) carries the slope?
       d log sigma_V / d log B = -1.852 +- 0.051   (x2 in alpha_vir)
       d log R       / d log B = -0.672 +- 0.107   (x-1)
       d log Sigma   / d log B = -3.188 +- 0.072   (x-1)
       d log sigma_V / d |cos l| = +0.248 +- 0.013  -- clouds seen along the LONG
         inner-Galaxy CO path have systematically larger line widths, which is blending, and
         inner-Galaxy means small R_gal means small B.  That is the source of the -2.7.

