======================================================================================================================
VERDICT (canonical footing)
======================================================================================================================
  [LAW PASSES] shape test 1: alpha_vir does NOT depend on the cloud's own acceleration, as the saturation law requires (data within 3 sigma of the SATURATED mock)   (0.2 sigma from saturated, 5.7 from isolated MOND, 0.5 from Newton)
  [LAW PASSES] shape test 1 also excludes the RESTATEMENT branch (isolated MOND, i.e. what v^4 = G M_b a_0 alone implies) at >= 3 sigma   (5.7 sigma)
  [NO VERDICT ] shape test 2 (the Galactocentric lever) is UNIDENTIFIED: the matched-cell slope -2.734 +- 0.099 excludes BOTH hypotheses, so it is measuring line-of-sight blending, not gravity.  Recorded as a dead estimator.

  >>> 2 of 2 scoreable law tests pass.
  >>> The clouds CONFIRM that the external-field effect must be switched on -- isolated MOND, which
      is exactly what v^4 = G M_b a_0 plus algebra gives, is excluded at 5.7 sigma --
      but they CANNOT separate the saturation law from Newton, because at g_ext ~ 2 a_0 the predicted
      boost is only 0.07 dex, well under the scatter.  Molecular clouds are a test of the EFE's
      EXISTENCE, not a measurement of its size.

  UPSILON LEVER, numerically:  d log alpha_vir / d log Upsilon_star = 0.000 EXACTLY.  Molecular
  clouds contain no starlight in the mass budget; the whole mass is CO-derived.  The lever that
  replaces it is d log alpha_vir / d log X_CO = -1.000, and X_CO carries a factor-2 uncertainty and
  a Galactocentric METALLICITY GRADIENT.  That gradient makes X_CO RISE outward, which makes M rise
  outward, which makes alpha_vir FALL outward -- the OPPOSITE sign to the saturation law's rise.  So
  the dominant systematic of shape test 2 works against the law, not for it.

RESULT: 2 checks, 0 FAIL   rc=0
